# VOYA Project Rules

These rules apply to the VOYA static frontend project: `index.html`, `style.css`, `script.js`, documentation, and image/animation work.

## Scope control

- Follow the approved phase plan.
- Do not begin a later phase early.
- Make the smallest complete change for the current phase.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Preserve existing menu, cart, WhatsApp, and navigation behavior unless the phase explicitly changes it.
- Inspect neighboring code before introducing a new pattern.
- Do not add dependencies unless explicitly required by the approved phase.

## Brand protection

- Preserve VOYA colors, typography, tone, illustrations, faces, glasses, proportions, line weight, and character identity.
- Characters remain 2D illustrations.
- Use layered 2D animation for character movement.
- Do not convert characters to true 3D.
- Plates, cups, food, ingredients, steam, shadows, and background elements may use depth-like 2D transforms.
- Do not generate guessed character angles or redesign missing body parts.

## Frontend quality

- Prefer native HTML, CSS, and JavaScript.
- Reuse existing project patterns.
- Keep menu and cart data in one source of truth.
- The latest menu selection must win during rapid switching.
- Cancel or replace stale transitions.
- Keep functions focused and naming clear.
- Do not leave dead code, debug logs, commented-out experiments, or unused assets.

## Accessibility

- Preserve semantic HTML.
- All interactive controls must be keyboard accessible.
- Focus states must be visible.
- Images must have appropriate alternative text.
- Maintain readable contrast and text size.
- Support `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- Do not make essential content dependent on animation.

## Responsive behavior

- Verify desktop and mobile layouts.
- Avoid horizontal overflow.
- Avoid clipped characters, menus, buttons, and cart content.
- Do not rely only on hover.
- Scroll-driven scenes must have a simpler mobile behavior when required.

## Performance

- Optimize large images.
- Use suitable WebP, PNG, or SVG formats.
- Avoid unnecessary transparent canvas space.
- Use lazy loading for below-the-fold images where appropriate.
- Prevent layout shifts by defining dimensions or aspect ratios.
- Animate `transform` and `opacity` where possible.
- Avoid scroll handlers that repeatedly trigger layout calculations.
- No true 3D library unless a later approved requirement proves it necessary.

## Security

- No secrets, credentials, API keys, or private data in committed files.
- Escape or safely insert dynamic text.
- Avoid unsafe `innerHTML` for untrusted content.
- External windows must use `noopener,noreferrer`.
- Validate generated WhatsApp text and URL encoding.
